  "reason": "No experiments are completed yet, so the key uncertainty is whether a simple unimodal baseline already performs well and what reference performance level is needed before adding complexity. config_001 tests the minimal RNA-only, single-profile, PCA baseline, establishing a low-complexity anchor for RNA representation and for later comparisons to multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders, image-only models, and multimodal fusion. It is the best first experiment under a limited budget because it is cheap, interpretable, and creates a clean baseline to isolate later design effects instead of confounding modality, profile, encoder, and fusion choices in one complex run."
}

